-# Bullpen's Private Key Import Incident Tests Trust in Non-Custodial Trading
+# What Bullpen's Private Key Import Incident Reveals About Non-Custodial Trading
 
 ## TL;DR
 
-I think Bullpen is more likely to restrict wallet imports in stages. It has permanently shut down the affected 2024 beta system. It could bring supported imports under Turnkey signing policies, strengthen passkey or two-factor authentication (2FA) by default, and use withdrawal allowlists, limits, and delays for large transfers. The incident tests what a login can authorize and whether users will still leave money in the terminal. The appeal of points and a potential airdrop depends on the same trust.
+Bullpen is more likely to restrict wallet imports in stages. It has permanently shut down the affected 2024 beta system. It could bring supported imports under Turnkey signing policies, strengthen passkey or two-factor authentication (2FA) by default, and use withdrawal allowlists, limits, and delays for large transfers. The incident tests what a login can authorize and whether users will still leave money in the terminal. The appeal of points and a potential airdrop depends on the same trust.
 
 ## What we know about the incident
 
-Bullpen initially reported **18–19 affected accounts** on November 24. The accounts were opened in its early beta from **April to June 2024**. On November 25 it confirmed **19**, including co-founder Ansem and 18 other testers. The company said the preliminary group represented less than **0.005%** of registered accounts and that **99.8%** of the funds taken came from one account. If the percentage also applies to the final count of 19, it implies more than **380,000** registered accounts. The preliminary low count of 18 implies a lower bound of **360,000**. Those are implied counts. Some early reports put losses around **$2 million**. Bitquery traced around **$2.57 million in USDC** along the path from Ansem's wallet. [Bullpen initial report](https://x.com/BullpenFi/status/2125267130870272331) · [99.8% update](https://x.com/BullpenFi/status/2125314571158073654) [Bitquery](https://bitquery.io/investigations/ansem-solana-wallet-drain)
