 ## What changes in the competitive position?
 
-DefiLlama's snapshot through November 27 showed **$15,279 in fees over 30 days**, or about **$186,000 a year** using **365/30**. October 2026 fees were **$23,982**, down roughly **85%** from **$161,631** in October 2025. Fees in the fourth quarter of 2026 were about **$36,551 through November 26**. The full fourth quarter of 2025 was about **$314,616**. Perpetual futures notional volume was **$33.66 million over 30 days** and **$2.487 billion lifetime**. The October comparison shows activity was slowing before the incident. The partial and full quarters cover different windows. The incident could accelerate that slowdown, and the next readings will show whether it has. [DefiLlama](https://defillama.com/protocol/bullpen)
